 {name:'Mahabalipuram',img:'tn-mahabalipuram',scene:'shore',km:'60 km from Chennai',time:'About 1.5 hours by road',season:'November to February',ease:'Gentle',text:'A UNESCO World Heritage Site on the Bay of Bengal, famous for the eighth-century Shore Temple, the Five Rathas and giant rock carvings. Paths are mostly flat and short, and there are plenty of shaded places to rest. It is an ideal first outing after treatment, and you can be back at your hotel the same evening.'},
 {name:'Kanchipuram',img:'tn-kanchipuram',scene:'temple',km:'75 km from Chennai',time:'About 2 hours by road',season:'October to March',ease:'Gentle',text:'Known as the city of a thousand temples and the home of hand-woven Kanchipuram silk. You can watch weavers at work on traditional looms and choose a silk saree or fabric to take home. Temple visits involve some walking barefoot, so your guide plans short, comfortable stops.'},
 {name:'Thanjavur',img:'tn-thanjavur',scene:'temple',km:'350 km from Chennai',time:'About 1 hour by flight to Tiruchirappalli, then 1 hour by road',season:'October to March',ease:'Moderate',text:'Home of the Brihadeeswarar Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site built over a thousand years ago by the Chola kings. Its great tower and peaceful lawns are best seen in the soft light of early morning or late afternoon. Thanjavur is also known for classical music, bronze sculpture and Thanjavur paintings.'},
 {name:'Madurai',img:'tn-madurai',scene:'temple',km:'460 km from Chennai',time:'About 1.5 hours by flight',season:'October to March',ease:'Moderate',text:'One of the oldest living cities in India, centred on the Meenakshi Amman Temple with its towering, colourful gateways. The temple complex is large, so your guide plans a route with seated breaks. Madurai is also famous for its markets, jasmine flowers and local food.'},
 {name:'Ooty',img:'tn-ooty',scene:'hills',km:'In the Nilgiri hills',time:'Flight to Coimbatore, then about 3 hours by road',season:'March to June, September to November',ease:'Moderate',text:'A cool hill station surrounded by tea gardens, pine forests and botanical gardens. The Nilgiri Mountain Railway, a UNESCO heritage train, offers a slow, scenic ride through the hills without any walking effort. The fresh mountain air makes Ooty a popular choice for a restful longer recovery stay.'},
 {name:'Kodaikanal',img:'tn-kodaikanal',scene:'hills',km:'In the Palani hills',time:'Flight to Madurai, then about 3.5 hours by road',season:'April to June, September to October',ease:'Moderate',text:'A quiet lake town in the clouds, with pine forests, gentle walking paths and calm boat rides on Kodaikanal Lake. The pace here is slow and peaceful. It suits patients who want a few restful days in cool weather before flying home.'},
 {name:'Kanyakumari',img:'tn-kanyakumari',scene:'shore',km:'At India\u2019s southern tip',time:'Flight to Thiruvananthapuram, then about 2.5 hours by road',season:'October to March',ease:'Moderate',text:'The southern tip of India, where the Arabian Sea, the Indian Ocean and the Bay of Bengal meet. Visitors come for sunrise and sunset over the ocean, and a short ferry ride to the Vivekananda Rock Memorial. Viewing points are easy to reach, and your guide times visits to avoid crowds.'},
 {name:'Rameswaram',img:'tn-rameswaram',scene:'shore',km:'570 km from Chennai',time:'Flight to Madurai, then about 3.5 hours by road',season:'October to April',ease:'Moderate',text:'An island town reached by the scenic Pamban Bridge across turquoise sea. It is known for the Ramanathaswamy Temple with its long, pillared corridors. The drive itself is a highlight, so this trip suits patients who are comfortable with longer road journeys.'},
 {name:'Chettinad',img:'tn-chettinad',scene:'heritage',km:'Near Karaikudi',time:'Flight to Madurai, then about 2 hours by road',season:'October to March',ease:'Gentle',text:'A region of grand heritage mansions with carved wooden pillars, courtyards and hand-made Athangudi tiles. Several mansions have become boutique heritage hotels where you can rest in comfort. Chettinad is also famous for its rich, aromatic cuisine, adjusted to your dietary needs.'},
 {name:'Yelagiri',img:'tn-yelagiri',scene:'hills',km:'230 km from Chennai',time:'About 4 hours by road',season:'All year',ease:'Gentle',text:'A small, peaceful hill station within driving distance of Chennai, with winding roads, orchards and a quiet lake. It is far less crowded than larger hill stations. Yelagiri is a good choice for a short, restful break when you do not want to take another flight.'}
